{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  Bottle → dish, rebuilt against design-reference/pairing.html.

  What the previous build got wrong, top to bottom — all of it visible in the
  design side by side:

  - THE BAND WAS DARK. The design makes this a light grey island (#c9c7c2,
    ruled top and bottom) sitting in the near-black page, the same move the
    Somm makes. The build rendered it as an ordinary dark .non-section, which
    is most of why it did not read like the design at all.
  - THE HEADING HIERARCHY WAS INVERTED. "Bottle → dish" is the small mono
    eyebrow in the design and "Already got the bottle. Now cook for it." is the
    52px statement. The build printed the eyebrow as the <h2> and the statement
    as small meta text beside it — exactly backwards.
  - THE STANDFIRST DID NOT EXIST. The design carries a paragraph explaining the
    reverse flow. There was no setting for it and nothing rendered.
  - THERE WAS NO WRITE BUTTON AND NO TRACE. The whole conceit is that the somm
    *writes* the dish — it reasons out loud, numbered, then the recipe lands.
    The build just swapped a hidden article in with no beat between, so the
    page asserted a recipe rather than composing one.
  - THE PANEL HAD NO EDGE. The design draws the recipe as one bordered box with
    a ruled spine between method and shopping list. The build had two loose
    columns floating on the page.
  - THE CTAs WERE IN THE WRONG COLUMN. The design pins "add" and "write me
    another" to the bottom of the shopping list, where someone who has just
    read the ingredients is looking. The build put "write me another" under the
    method and dropped a full product-card into the aside — a dark card on what
    should be a light panel.

  Recipes live in the non_recipe metaobject; see docs/recipes.md.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign recipes = section.settings.recipes.value | default: shop.metaobjects.non_recipe.values
  assign efforts = 'fast,sunday,showoff,aperitivo,sweet' | split: ','
-%}

<section
  class="non-recipes"
  data-non-recipes
  data-trace-speed="{{ section.settings.trace_speed | default: 340 }}"
  {% if section.settings.band_bg != blank %}style="--non-recipes-bg: {{ section.settings.band_bg }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="non-recipes__inner">
    {%- comment -%}
      Eyebrow, statement, standfirst. Three levels, in the design's order.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="non-recipes__head">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow non-recipes__kicker">{{ section.settings.heading }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="non-recipes__title">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.standfirst != blank -%}
        <p class="non-recipes__stand">{{ section.settings.standfirst }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if recipes.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Both pickers and the write button on one baseline, as the design has
        them — the row reads as a single instrument rather than three stacked
        controls.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-recipes__controls">
        <div class="non-recipes__group">
          <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.bottle_label }}</span>
          <div class="non-filters" role="group" aria-label="{{ section.settings.bottle_label | escape }}">
            {%- assign seen = '' -%}
            {%- for recipe in recipes -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign bottle = recipe.bottle.value
                assign key = bottle.handle
                assign marker = '|' | append: key | append: '|'
              -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Two nested tests, NOT `key != blank and seen contains marker ==
                false`. Liquid has no boolean negation of `contains`: chaining
                `== false` onto it is a parse error, and Shopify rejects the
                whole file for it — silently, keeping the previous version.

                This is what froze this section on the 31 July build while three
                later pushes reported success. It only survived that long
                because Shopify validates on WRITE, so the bad line sat happily
                in an already-accepted file and only bit when the file was next
                pushed. snippets/non-code.liquid:22 documents the same trap; the
                note never made it here. check.py rule 1d now catches it.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if key != blank -%}
              {%- unless seen contains marker -%}
                {%- assign seen = seen | append: marker -%}
                {%- capture bcode %}{% render 'non-code', product: bottle %}{% endcapture -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="non-filter"
                  data-non-recipe-bottle="{{ key }}"
                  aria-pressed="false">
                  {{ bcode | strip }}
                </button>
              {%- endunless -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="non-recipes__group">
          <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.effort_label }}</span>
          <div class="non-filters" role="group" aria-label="{{ section.settings.effort_label | escape }}">
            {%- for effort in efforts -%}
              <button
                type="button"
                class="non-filter"
                data-non-recipe-effort="{{ effort }}"
                aria-pressed="false">
                {%- case effort -%}
                  {%- when 'fast' -%}{{ section.settings.effort_fast }}
                  {%- when 'sunday' -%}{{ section.settings.effort_sunday }}
                  {%- when 'showoff' -%}{{ section.settings.effort_showoff }}
                  {%- when 'aperitivo' -%}{{ section.settings.effort_aperitivo }}
                  {%- else -%}{{ section.settings.effort_sweet }}
                {%- endcase -%}
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>

        <button type="button" class="non-recipes__write" data-non-recipe-write>
          {{ section.settings.write_label }}
        </button>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The trace. Filled by recipes.js from the lines below, one at a time,
        while the panel is held back. Server-rendered rather than built in JS so
        the copy is editable and so it exists with JS off — recipes.js only
        reveals it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.trace != blank -%}
        <div class="non-recipes__trace" data-non-recipe-trace hidden aria-live="polite">
          {%- assign lines = section.settings.trace | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
          {%- for line in lines -%}
            {%- assign clean = line | strip -%}
            {%- if clean != blank -%}
              <div class="non-recipes__traceline" data-non-recipe-traceline hidden>
                <span class="non-mono non-recipes__tracen">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
                <span>{{ clean }}</span>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Every recipe is rendered, but only one is ever visible. They are marked
        hidden in Liquid rather than by JS so the page never flashes all thirty.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-recipe__slot">
        {%- for recipe in recipes -%}
          {%- assign bottle = recipe.bottle.value -%}
          {%- capture code %}{% render 'non-code', product: bottle %}{% endcapture -%}
          <article
            class="non-recipe"
            data-non-recipe
            data-bottle="{{ bottle.handle }}"
            data-effort="{{ recipe.effort | downcase | strip }}"
            hidden>
            <div class="non-recipe__main">
              <div>
                {%- if recipe.meta != blank -%}
                  <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ recipe.meta }}</div>
                {%- endif -%}
                <h3 class="non-recipe__title">{{ recipe.title }}</h3>
                {%- if recipe.intro != blank -%}
                  <p class="non-recipe__intro">{{ recipe.intro }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

              {%- if recipe.steps.value.size > 0 -%}
                <div class="non-recipe__part">
                  <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.method_label }}</div>
                  <ol class="non-steps non-recipe__steps">
                    {%- for step in recipe.steps.value -%}
                      <li class="non-step">
                        <div class="non-step__n">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</div>
                        <p class="non-step__b" style="margin:0">{{ step }}</p>
                      </li>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </ol>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if recipe.why != blank -%}
                <div class="non-recipe__why">
                  <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">
                    {{ section.settings.why_label }}{% if code != blank %} {{ code | strip }}{% endif %}
                  </div>
                  <p class="non-recipe__whyb">{{ recipe.why }}</p>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            <aside class="non-recipe__aside">
              {%- comment -%}
                Flush to the top of the column and 4/3, as the design has it.
                No entry carries an image yet (docs/recipes.md), so the bed
                shows rather than a collapsed column.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="non-recipe__media">
                {%- if recipe.image != blank -%}
                  {{
                    recipe.image.value
                    | image_url: width: 900
                    | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '420,640,900',
                      class: 'non-recipe__img', alt: recipe.title
                  }}
                {%- elsif bottle.featured_image != blank -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    Falls back to the BOTTLE's own shot. All thirty non_recipe
                    entries have an empty `image` field (docs/recipes.md), so
                    this slot was a bare grey rectangle on every recipe — which
                    reads as a broken image, not as a missing one. The bottle is
                    honest: it is the thing the dish was written around, and it
                    is the one photograph guaranteed to exist. Replace it per
                    recipe by filling the metaobject's image field; nothing here
                    changes when you do.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {{
                    bottle.featured_image
                    | image_url: width: 900
                    | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '420,640,900',
                      class: 'non-recipe__img', alt: bottle.title
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

              <div class="non-recipe__panel">
                <div class="non-recipe__listhead">
                  <span class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.list_label }}</span>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    There is no `serves` field on the metaobject today, so this
                    renders nothing rather than inventing a number. Add the
                    field and it appears — no template change needed.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- if recipe.serves != blank -%}
                    <span class="non-mono non-recipe__serves">{{ recipe.serves }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>

                {%- if recipe.ingredients.value.size > 0 -%}
                  <div class="non-recipe__list">
                    {%- for line in recipe.ingredients.value -%}
                      {%- assign parts = line | split: ' — ' -%}
                      <div class="non-recipe__ing">
                        <span>{{ parts | first }}</span>
                        {%- if parts.size > 1 -%}
                          <span class="non-mono non-recipe__qty">{{ parts | last }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </div>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}

                <div class="non-recipe__ctas">
                  {%- if bottle != blank -%}
                    <a class="non-recipe__add" href="{{ bottle.url }}">
                      {{ section.settings.add_label }}{% if code != blank %} {{ code | strip }}{% endif %}
                    </a>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <button type="button" class="non-recipe__again" data-non-recipe-another>
                    {{ section.settings.another_label }}
                  </button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </article>
        {%- endfor -%}

        <p class="non-recipes__empty" data-non-recipe-empty hidden>
          {{ section.settings.empty_text }}
        </p>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="non-recipes__empty">
        No recipes yet. Create <code>non_recipe</code> metaobject entries — see docs/recipes.md.
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{ 'recipes.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
